    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31671" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ob-lectātĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				delighting, delight</i> (a favorite word of Cic.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">indagatio ipsa habet oblectationem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Ac. 2, 41, 127</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">animi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					de Or. 1, 26, 118</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">curarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Off.
					2, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vitae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fin. 5, 19, 53</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">requies plena oblectationis fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Lael. 27, 103</span></i>
			.</div>
